    "content": "House Financial Services Committee Chair French Hill stated that current regulations from the SEC and CFTC are insufficient compared to the permanent changes the CLARITY Act would provide. He expressed hope that Congress will pass the legislation during the upcoming lame duck session before a new Congress takes office.",
